preConditionHook:
// SUCCESSIVE TREND LINES LOSING SLOPE (T13-09) -- Brooks's maturing,
// weakening trend. LONG reads the BULL trend line, drawn as slice B01 and B02
// draw every line in the corpus: through the two most recent CONFIRMED swing
// LOWS. The PRIOR line is the pair one pivot back, so the comparison is three
// pivots wide. SHORT is the mirror on the bear trend line through the swing
// HIGHS.
//
// THE CONSTRUCTION DECISION IS WHAT MAKES THIS CODEABLE. The mined candidate
// was graded research because it assumed a persisted history of redrawn lines
// and a rule for when a redraw happens. Under B01's construction the current
// line is ALWAYS the newest confirmed pivot pair, so no history is kept: the
// prior line is pivots 2 and 3, the current line pivots 1 and 2.
//
// MEASURED, EL_TLValue_Probe.txt: TLValue(P1, B1, P2, B2, target) is the pure
// two-point line anchored at the FIRST pair, Slope = (P2 - P1) / (B2 - B1).
// Only the SLOPE is wanted here, so that quotient is written out rather than
// differencing two TLValue calls; it is TLValue's own arithmetic, on the same
// doubles. THE BAR-NUMBER CONVENTION IS THE CALLER'S -- the probe measured
// bars-ago and CurrentBar-relative spellings of the identical line agreeing
// at drift 0 on all 19,492 bars -- and the CurrentBar-relative one is used
// here (bar number = minus bars-ago) so the slope comes out per FORWARD bar
// and a rising bull line reads POSITIVE. With the older pivot as the first
// anchor that is (newer price - older price) / (older bars-ago - newer
// bars-ago), the spelling below. Bar1 = Bar2 does NOT halt, it silently
// returns 0.0, so haveLoLines / haveHiLines guard the pivot bars as distinct
// before any division, and both slopes stay 0.0 when the guard fails.
//
// FLATTENING. Long: the older line rose (loOldSlope > 0) and the newer one
// rises less than flattenFraction of it. Short: the older line fell
// (hiOldSlope < 0) and the newer one falls less steeply, which with two
// negative numbers is hiNewSlope > flattenFraction * hiOldSlope. The newer
// slope is NOT required to keep its sign -- a line that has rolled over is
// more than flat, and the merged pseudocode carries no such term.
//
// THE PIVOT SCAN IS INLINED rather than calling SwingLowBar / SwingLow at
// Occurrence 1, 2 and 3. The register's swinghigh / swinglow / swinghighbar /
// swinglowbar rows are VERIFIED but list Occurrence 3+ explicitly as
// UNMEASURED, and the third pivot is the whole comparison. Slice B02 blocked
// this rule on that; the inlined scan is the route ratified for a third or
// later pivot, since plain EL loops and comparisons are registered and the
// scan reproduces the MEASURED pivot test exactly (EL_Swing_Probe.txt /
// el_swing_output1.txt, @ES 60 min):
//
//   * the pivot bar is AT OR ABOVE the swingStrength OLDER bars and STRICTLY
//     ABOVE the swingStrength NEWER bars, so a flat top yields exactly ONE
//     pivot, the LATER of the equal bars. Bars-ago indexing makes the SMALLER
//     index the NEWER bar, so the strict half is the k < j loop (el_gt) and
//     the at-or-above half the k > j loop (el_ge);
//   * the confirmation lag is exactly swingStrength bars -- the scan starts
//     at j = swingStrength and that lag is what makes it lookahead-safe;
//   * candidate offsets run 0 .. Length - 1 from the current bar INCLUSIVE,
//     so j stops at pivotLookback - 1, while the neighbourhood test reaches
//     swingStrength bars PAST the window: deepest bar touched is
//     pivotLookback - 1 + swingStrength;
//   * the bars-ago count the scan records is the same plain count
//     SwingLowBar returns, in swingStrength .. pivotLookback - 1;
//   * the comparisons carry the 2.22e-12 relational tolerance, hence el_gt /
//     el_ge / el_lt / el_le rather than raw > and >=;
//   * prices and bars start at the -1 SENTINEL and every use is gated on the
//     count reaching 3 -- -1 as a PRICE sits under every real price;
//   * the low side's TIE sense is the mirror of the measured high-side rule
//     rather than an observation, as the swinglow row records.
//
// No WFSafe_SwingHigh exists in MultiWalk, so plain EL governs. Written
// without an early break, matching the EL twin statement for statement:
// Break is not a registered word, so the loops run to the end and the `< 3`
// guards stop a fourth pivot being recorded. pivotLookback(40) was added
// because the merged parameters omitted the window; it is wider than the
// two-pivot families' 20 because a THIRD pivot must fit.
//
// No scratch is declared at hook scope -- every value below is a
// localVariables entry -- because this rule may be placed twice in one
// strategy and its hooks emitted twice into the one class.
nHiPiv = 0;
nLoPiv = 0;
hiPx1 = -1.0;
hiPx2 = -1.0;
hiPx3 = -1.0;
hiBar1 = -1.0;
hiBar2 = -1.0;
hiBar3 = -1.0;
loPx1 = -1.0;
loPx2 = -1.0;
loPx3 = -1.0;
loBar1 = -1.0;
loBar2 = -1.0;
loBar3 = -1.0;
for (int j = (int)swingStrength; j <= (int)pivotLookback - 1; ++j) {
    bool okHi = true;
    bool okLo = true;
    for (int k = j - (int)swingStrength; k < j; ++k) {
        if (!el_gt(high[j], high[k])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_lt(low[j], low[k])) okLo = false;
    }
    for (int k = j + 1; k <= j + (int)swingStrength; ++k) {
        if (!el_ge(high[j], high[k])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_le(low[j], low[k])) okLo = false;
    }
    if (okHi && nHiPiv < 3) {
        nHiPiv = nHiPiv + 1;
        if (nHiPiv == 1) { hiPx1 = high[j]; hiBar1 = (double)j; }
        if (nHiPiv == 2) { hiPx2 = high[j]; hiBar2 = (double)j; }
        if (nHiPiv == 3) { hiPx3 = high[j]; hiBar3 = (double)j; }
    }
    if (okLo && nLoPiv < 3) {
        nLoPiv = nLoPiv + 1;
        if (nLoPiv == 1) { loPx1 = low[j]; loBar1 = (double)j; }
        if (nLoPiv == 2) { loPx2 = low[j]; loBar2 = (double)j; }
        if (nLoPiv == 3) { loPx3 = low[j]; loBar3 = (double)j; }
    }
}
haveLoLines = (nLoPiv == 3) && (loBar1 != loBar2) && (loBar2 != loBar3);
haveHiLines = (nHiPiv == 3) && (hiBar1 != hiBar2) && (hiBar2 != hiBar3);
loNewSlope = 0.0;
loOldSlope = 0.0;
hiNewSlope = 0.0;
hiOldSlope = 0.0;
if (haveLoLines) {
    loNewSlope = (loPx1 - loPx2) / (loBar2 - loBar1);
    loOldSlope = (loPx2 - loPx3) / (loBar3 - loBar2);
}
if (haveHiLines) {
    hiNewSlope = (hiPx1 - hiPx2) / (hiBar2 - hiBar1);
    hiOldSlope = (hiPx2 - hiPx3) / (hiBar3 - hiBar2);
}
